# Copy to .env and fill in. `.env` is git-ignored (*.env in .gitignore).
# This file configures the server itself, which always runs on the host via
# `go run .`. docker-compose.local.yml runs the database only and reads nothing
# from here, so a stale value cannot repoint the container.

# ─── Database ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CockroachDB Cloud, or any Postgres with the pgvector extension.
#
# Against the local stack, the container ports are published — use localhost,
# with the port of whichever database you started:
#   CockroachDB: postgresql://root@localhost:26257/defaultdb?sslmode=disable
#   PostgreSQL:  postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/agent_space?sslmode=disable
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host:26257/defaultdb?sslmode=verify-full

# ─── LLM (any OpenAI-compatible endpoint) ────────────────────────────────────
# One variable names each model, wherever it runs. OPENROUTER_MODEL is sent to
# a local server unchanged, so switching endpoints does not mean switching
# settings.

OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-...
OPENROUTER_MODEL=z-ai/glm-5.2
# OPENROUTER_EMBEDDING_MODEL=qwen/qwen3-embedding-8b
# OPENROUTER_EMBEDDING_DIMENSIONS=1024

# ── Run chat against your own server ──
# OPENAI_BASE_URL moves CHAT ONLY. Embeddings stay on OpenRouter, because the
# vector column is sized to the embedder at CREATE TABLE: moving chat to a local
# model must not silently swap a 1024-wide embedder for a 768-wide one and
# invalidate every stored vector. Chat is the expensive half worth running
# locally; embeddings are ~$0.01 per million tokens.
#
#   OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1          # Ollama
#   OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000/v1           # vLLM
#   OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080/v1           # llama.cpp, LM Studio
#
# From inside a container, a server on your host is host.docker.internal:
#   OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434/v1
#
# Set OPENROUTER_MODEL to whatever name your server answers to. Leave it empty
# and "local-model" is sent: servers that serve one loaded model ignore the
# field, but ones that route by name (Ollama, vLLM) will reject it.
#
# The key is optional here — most local servers ignore it. OPENAI_API_KEY or
# LLM_API_KEY are used if set; OPENROUTER_API_KEY deliberately is not, so a live
# billable credential is never forwarded to an arbitrary process on localhost.
#   OPENAI_API_KEY=whatever-your-server-wants

# ── Run embeddings somewhere else too (fully offline) ──
# Only then does the request-width handling change: the OpenAI `dimensions`
# field is omitted, because most self-hosted embedding servers reject it, and
# the column width has to be stated instead (nomic-embed-text is 768,
# mxbai-embed-large 1024).
#   EMBEDDING_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
#   OPENROUTER_EMBEDDING_MODEL=nomic-embed-text
#   VECTOR_DIMENSIONS=768
#
# If your server does accept the field, opt back in and it sizes the column too:
#   OPENROUTER_EMBEDDING_DIMENSIONS=768
#
# Changing the width means recreating the tables:
#   go run ./cmd/nuke -mode=drop

# ─── CockroachDB MCP (the second CockroachDB integration) ────────────────────
# Cloud: create a service account API key in the Cloud Console under Access
# Management. COCKROACH_CLUSTER_ID is optional and scopes the agent to one
# cluster; omit it and the key's full RBAC scope applies.
COCKROACH_API_KEY=
COCKROACH_CLUSTER_ID=
# COCKROACH_MCP_URL=https://cockroachlabs.cloud/mcp

# Local: docker-compose.local.yml runs a self-hosted MCP server alongside
# CockroachDB. Point the server at it with:
#   COCKROACH_MCP_URL=http://localhost:8443
#   COCKROACH_API_KEY=local-dev-token-insecure   # = LOCAL_MCP_TOKEN below
#   COCKROACH_CLUSTER_ID=          # must be empty: scoping is a Cloud concept
#
# Leave COCKROACH_API_KEY empty and /tools and /agent report 503; the rest of
# the API works. That is also what happens on the pgvector-only path, since the
# MCP server reads crdb_internal and cannot talk to PostgreSQL.
#
# Overrides the local MCP server's bearer token. Minimum 16 characters — the
# server exits at boot if it is shorter.
# LOCAL_MCP_TOKEN=local-dev-token-insecure

# The agent is offered only the read-only MCP tools, so a wrong tool call cannot
# drop a table. Set this to hand it the write tools as well. Leave it unset.
# AGENT_ALLOW_WRITE_TOOLS=false

# Read-only tools the agent is nonetheless not offered, comma-separated.
# Defaults to show_statement,show_running_queries: cluster introspection that
# the prompt already discourages, and that does not return inside the client's
# 90s ceiling on a Cloud Basic cluster. Set it empty to offer everything.
# AGENT_EXCLUDE_TOOLS=show_statement,show_running_queries

# ─── API access ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Shared secret for /store, /retrieve, /ask and /agent. /ping and /tools stay
# open. REQUIRED before exposing this server publicly: one /agent run is on the
# order of 15k tokens against a billable key, and /retrieve reads stored
# incidents back out. Unset means no authentication at all, which the server
# warns about at boot.
#
# Clients send it as `X-Agent-Token: <token>` (or `Authorization: Bearer`).
# scripts/demo.sh and scripts/bench.sh pick it up from API_TOKEN automatically.
# API_TOKEN=
